<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tashfin ibn Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1145</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tashfin ibn Ali was emir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> from 1143 to 1145, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-yusuf">Ali ibn Yusuf</a>. Earlier governor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, where he campaigned against the Christian kingdoms, he came to the throne as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-mumin">Abd al-Mu'min</a> were overrunning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. Besieged at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a>, he died in 1145 when his horse fell from a cliff as he tried to escape, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> fell to the Almohads two years later.</p></div>
